From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:04:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: sample encoder GPU time and pipeline limits with
 MESA_KK_PASS_PROF

Sample two submitted frames every 1200 presents (first 600). Keep one-shot commands only while profiling and replay selected submissions, including the WSI blit. Resolve after present and every completion; discard incomplete/overflow/error frames. Capture disables allocation entirely.

Compute profiling uses precise samples; Vulkan queries retain relaxed sampling. Native-copy/empty and mixed copy+dispatch costs are unavailable, not zero (owner-approved scope; PLA-474). Assemble each pass before one fd write because Wine logging bypasses the stdio stream lock.

Log pipeline MSL hashes, Metal thread limits, static threadgroup bytes and the descriptor thread cap. These are not register or spill counts; no compile hints are changed.

Linear: PLA-466
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-29-kk-pass-prof.md
Offered-upstream: no
